  "descriptionRussian": "Распространённые неправильные глаголы в настоящем времени",
  "imageName": "exclamationmark.triangle.fill",
  "intro": "Some common Russian verbs don't follow the regular conjugation patterns. These irregular verbs must be memorized. The good news is that the most common verbs (want, eat, give, go) are used so frequently that you'll learn them quickly through practice.",
  "rules": [
    "Хотеть (to want) mixes both conjugations: хочу, хочешь, хочет, хотим, хотите, хотят.",
    "Есть (to eat) is fully irregular: ем, ешь, ест, едим, едите, едят.",
    "Пить (to drink) has a consonant change: пью, пьёшь, пьёт, пьём, пьёте, пьют.",
    "Быть (to be) has NO present tense forms in Russian - simply omit it: Я студент (I am a student)."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Я хочу кофе. (I want coffee.)",
    "Он ест яблоко. (He is eating an apple.)",
    "Она пьёт чай. (She is drinking tea.)",
    "Я студент. (I am a student.), no verb 'to be'"
  ],
